          "short": "$\\frac{3}{x-2}$\n\nUse $x^2-4=(x-2)(x+2)$, then cancel the common factor.",
          "worked": "$x^2-4=(x-2)(x+2)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{x+2}+\\frac{2}{x-2}+\\frac{4}{x^2-4}&=\\frac{(x-2)+2(x+2)+4}{(x-2)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{1}{x+2}+\\frac{2}{x-2}+\\frac{4}{x^2-4}&=\\frac{3(x+2)}{(x-2)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{1}{x+2}+\\frac{2}{x-2}+\\frac{4}{x^2-4}&=\\frac{3}{x-2}\\end{align*}$$",
