        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{x+3}$\n\nUse $9-x^2=-(x-3)(x+3)$ before combining the numerators.",
          "worked": "$9-x^2=-(x-3)(x+3)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5}{3+x}+\\frac{2}{x-3}-\\frac{6-6x}{9-x^2}&=\\frac{5(x-3)+2(x+3)+(6-6x)}{(x-3)(x+3)}\\\\\\frac{5}{3+x}+\\frac{2}{x-3}-\\frac{6-6x}{9-x^2}&=\\frac{x-3}{(x-3)(x+3)}\\\\\\frac{5}{3+x}+\\frac{2}{x-3}-\\frac{6-6x}{9-x^2}&=\\frac{1}{x+3}\\end{align*}$$",
