        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{(1-2\\ell)^2}$\n\nFactorise the quadratic denominator and retain the repeated factor in the common denominator.",
          "worked": "$1-5\\ell+6\\ell^2=(1-2\\ell)(1-3\\ell)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2\\ell}{(1-2\\ell)^2}-\\frac{1-\\ell}{1-5\\ell+6\\ell^2}+\\frac{2}{1-3\\ell}&=\\frac{2\\ell(1-3\\ell)-(1-\\ell)(1-2\\ell)+2(1-2\\ell)^2}{(1-2\\ell)^2(1-3\\ell)}\\\\\\frac{2\\ell}{(1-2\\ell)^2}-\\frac{1-\\ell}{1-5\\ell+6\\ell^2}+\\frac{2}{1-3\\ell}&=\\frac{2\\ell-6\\ell^2-1+3\\ell-2\\ell^2+2-8\\ell+8\\ell^2}{(1-2\\ell)^2(1-3\\ell)}\\\\\\frac{2\\ell}{(1-2\\ell)^2}-\\frac{1-\\ell}{1-5\\ell+6\\ell^2}+\\frac{2}{1-3\\ell}&=\\frac{1-3\\ell}{(1-2\\ell)^2(1-3\\ell)}\\\\\\frac{2\\ell}{(1-2\\ell)^2}-\\frac{1-\\ell}{1-5\\ell+6\\ell^2}+\\frac{2}{1-3\\ell}&=\\frac{1}{(1-2\\ell)^2}\\end{align*}$$",
