          "short": "$\\frac{-1}{(p-1)(p-3)}$\n\nFactorise all three denominators, combine the fractions and cancel $p-2$.",
          "worked": "$p^2-4p+3=(p-1)(p-3)$, $p^2-3p+2=(p-1)(p-2)$ and $p^2-5p+6=(p-2)(p-3)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{p^2-4p+3}-\\frac{1}{p^2-3p+2}-\\frac{1}{p^2-5p+6}&=\\frac{(p-2)-(p-3)-(p-1)}{(p-1)(p-2)(p-3)}\\\\\\frac{1}{p^2-4p+3}-\\frac{1}{p^2-3p+2}-\\frac{1}{p^2-5p+6}&=\\frac{2-p}{(p-1)(p-2)(p-3)}\\\\\\frac{1}{p^2-4p+3}-\\frac{1}{p^2-3p+2}-\\frac{1}{p^2-5p+6}&=\\frac{-(p-2)}{(p-1)(p-2)(p-3)}\\\\\\frac{1}{p^2-4p+3}-\\frac{1}{p^2-3p+2}-\\frac{1}{p^2-5p+6}&=\\frac{-1}{(p-1)(p-3)}\\end{align*}$$",
